index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..1686beba8efc8df74914232199a9ca65c0c6e11d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/embedded-uniffi-bindgen-noop/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# No-op Kotlin bindings
+
+This generator emits pure Kotlin internal bindings for the Android Glean wrapper.
+It does not load a native library, invoke callbacks, record metrics or sessions,
+persist data, schedule work, or produce upload tasks. Session records are passive
+API data types only; event test getters always return an empty list.
+
+The hardcoded API targets Glean **68.0.1** (tag commit
+`92ecd18105fd2936e11936da749183369a491580`). The generator is not a general-purpose
+UniFFI replacement, and does not emit Python or Swift bindings.
+
+## Validation
+
+From the Glean source root:
+
+```sh
+cargo test --locked -p uniffi-bindgen-noop
+```
+
+
+The Rust tests check the current UDL's record fields, namespace functions, metric
+constructors/methods, callbacks, and Android configuration argument names against
+the generated Kotlin. A comment/whitespace-insensitive UDL snapshot catches other
+API changes, including defaults and enum variants. Review API compatibility and
+no-op behavior before updating `tests/glean-68.0.1.udl`; do not blindly refresh it.
+The snapshot does not make production generation reject unknown UDL revisions.
+
+An additional ignored test compiles and executes `tests/SessionNoop.kt` against
+freshly generated bindings. Supply these environment variables using an already
+installed JDK and Kotlin compiler (the test does not download tools):
+
+- `JAVA`: Java executable path.
+- `KOTLIN_COMPILER_CLASSPATH`: platform-separated classpath containing the Kotlin
+  embeddable compiler and its runtime dependencies, including annotations.
+- `KOTLIN_STDLIB`: path to the matching Kotlin standard-library JAR.
+
+Then run:
+
+```sh
+cargo test --locked -p uniffi-bindgen-noop kotlin_session_fixture_compiles_and_runs -- --ignored
+```
+
+The fixture covers all session modes before initialization, after initialization,
+and after shutdown; default/explicit end reasons; unsigned fields; nullable
+metadata; event suppression; attribution/distribution clearing; callback
+suppression; safe absent UUID getters; and upload termination even when uploading is enabled. It compiles
+and runs without Glean native code, JNA, Android, or network dependencies. Test
+output directories are created inside this crate and removed on completion.
+
+These focused tests do not replace compiling the complete Android wrapper. They
+do not test the generated UniFFI FFI/serialization machinery, which is deliberately
+absent, or prevent side effects introduced in code outside these bindings.
